    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 0.54,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.06,
    "rationale": "At 18 h, the diluted aliquots scale back to about the undiluted reading of 0.53. Dilutions of 5×, 10× and 30× give 0.52, 0.575 and 0.62 after correcting for dilution. If the plateau were caused by detector saturation, the diluted readings would scale back to much higher values. The 5 h aliquot read at 10× gives 0.524, which matches its undiluted reading of 0.529. This indicates the reader is linear in this range. The 30× result is noisy (0.52 and 0.72 from the two replicates), and the small upward drift across the dilutions is within that noise. The plateau reflects stationary phase."
  },
